<description>Consolidation of the Trident closure business rules for sn_vulc_result_group and sn_vulc_result. The four result-group rules (Trident Recopen From Resolved, BOFA Trident closure approval gate, BOFA Trident reopen window, BOFA Trident start workflow) are replaced by one rule, BOFA Trident closure lifecycle (before update, state changes, order 100), which runs the same governance in a fixed order: close gate (attachment required + approved closure request), reopen window check, closure request staging on Resolved, and cancellation of open approvals when a pending request is backed out. Root cause of the duplicated approvals: the old start workflow rule called TridentClosureUtil.requestClosure(current), which runs current.update() inside a before rule - the record was written twice per Resolve (nested write plus the original save) and the Trident Closure Approval flow trigger matched both writes, creating two approval sets. The new rule stages substate/approval on the current write only, so the record is written once and the flow runs once. Also fixed: missing Trident guard on the resolve path (non-Trident tasks are no longer touched), action.setRedirectURL removed from rule context, reopen window arithmetic in TridentClosureUtil.reopenAllowed (the window was added to today instead of counted back from the closure date, so reopening was never blocked), closure stamps now cleared when a Trident test result is reopened to any state, and approvals are cancelled on backout for non-interactive updates as well. TridentClosureUtil gains applyClosureRequest() (stage without update) and cancelOpenApprovals(); requestClosure() is kept for UI action use. Contains 7 updates: 4 business rule deletions, 1 new business rule, 1 business rule update (Trident reopen window (test result)), 1 script include update.</description>
